{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-syntomic}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a14280e4f7b16b0486e211007992cff05a384b6518a20d5fea9455184c8e9c3", "source_text": "The syntomic topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ad8526b56f54f1961057bf16bc2f6f3b2a290870265487511c66e188a8ed3350", "unit_id": "tag:0224:title"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f66aaba62f27af3d693f62e01cfa6b5803f9ba6e4af5451d7ac6a760574e643", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we define the syntomic topology.\nThis topology is quite interesting in that it often\nhas the same cohomology groups as the fppf topology\nbut is technically easier to deal with.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:37d57e409184c53511397f915bc8413115ef06888aad6506cdd0f4dd6f0df62b", "unit_id": "tag:0224:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$T = \\bigcup f_i(T_i)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-syntomic-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:283f9dea2be6a5f99e7e729bc3db42e6c914a1813f97c1b0e20c1ac32623e25a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c72539cf9ea3f7caa42fafb6b3c0028f0a5df3c969daab6952d303ce52d5264", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. An <TEXTITOPEN_0001>syntomic covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is syntomic and such\nthat <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:486bf93751dae40cdaf8c4bdc64780d383e5be657fa892b383cadd68aff2e1d4", "unit_id": "tag:0225:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:592dc0a72f0b0b3276565366a064ef78a4785a45917c0b7f41f1cabe2d567756", "source_text": "Any smooth covering is a syntomic covering, and a fortiori,\nany <ACCENT_0001>tale or Zariski covering is a syntomic covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5e992b61018e19a519ab5721940331afe1c17648721d9172c38a9b17b795b167", "unit_id": "tag:0226:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-smooth-syntomic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c94957271bef0da434160cd9aef72c395ef4278762967b4717f66e05d328232", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions and the fact that a smooth\nmorphism is syntomic, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:90f3b72314c422339a968963dc2f234ba1e181a60671aec41c5ee12b4bb16fbf", "unit_id": "tag:0226:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:943439cfb24e73189f5109525a32bbad0ee1182c274bf9d60e97cf92ef6020c4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we show that this notion satisfies the conditions of\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe60d7ff7dec91903335c151eda3e3489f64647b495bf10d622c43cc9afc0c89", "unit_id": "tag:0224:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6769921b618bfbc07202a68e5a71942865a43dd17f8a8dd9f1dd562b929e789c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis a syntomic covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is a syntomic covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have a syntomic covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is a syntomic covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is a syntomic covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is a syntomic covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b7c5eb4db1fb7346a1de21da3ab0c2cba0d190ac3233b9136ac79acb8f95255e", "unit_id": "tag:0227:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4860fb3167c3515d6fd2e465ac4d5019274b55d73a688edd92699f185606eca8", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:0227:proof"}
